actual_sparql:
PREFIX hyobs:  <https://w3id.org/hmontology/>
PREFIX geo:    <http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#>
PREFIX sosa:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/>
PREFIX qudt:   <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/>
PREFIX xsd:    <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>
PREFIX chebi:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_>
PREFIX envthes: <http://vocabs.lter-europe.net/EnvThes/>

SELECT ?topCatchment ?topMedian ?neighborCatchment
WHERE {
  GRAPH <hydroturtle/quadica> {
    {
      SELECT ?topCatchment (MAX(xsd:decimal(?val)) AS ?topMedian)
      WHERE {
        ?obs a sosa:Observation ;
            sosa:observedProperty hyobs:NO3NConcentrationMedian ;
            hyobs:hasAnalyte chebi:17632 ;
            sosa:hasFeatureOfInterest ?topCatchment ;
            sosa:resultTime ?t ;
            sosa:hasResult ?res .

        ?res qudt:numericValue ?val .

        FILTER(YEAR(?t) = 1999)
      }
      GROUP BY ?topCatchment
      ORDER BY DESC(?topMedian)
      LIMIT 1
    }

    ?topCatchment geo:hasGeometry ?g1 .
    ?g1 geo:asWKT ?wkt1 .

    ?neighborCatchment a envthes:30212.
    ?neighborCatchment geo:hasGeometry ?g2 .
    ?g2 geo:asWKT ?neighborWkt .

    FILTER(?neighborCatchment != ?topCatchment)
    FILTER(bif:st_intersects(?wkt1, ?neighborWkt, 0))
  }
}

reasoning_path_generated:
Reasoning path:  
?obs -rdf:type-> sosa:Observation -sosa:observedProperty-> hyobs:NO3NConcentrationMedian -sosa:madeBySensor-> ?sensor -hyobs:monitorsCatchment-> ?catchment -geo:hasGeometry-> ?catchmentGeom -geo:asWKT-> ?wkt ;  
?catchment -rdf:type-> envthes:30212 ;  
?catchment2 -rdf:type-> envthes:30212 -geo:hasGeometry-> ?catchment2Geom -geo:asWKT-> ?wkt2 ;  
?catchmentGeom and ?catchment2Geom are compared via a computed spatial boundary relation (shared boundary / touches) to identify neighboring catchments.

Interpretation:  
To answer the question, the path first finds the observation of annual median NO₃-N (mapped to `hyobs:NO3NConcentrationMedian`) and the sensor that made it, then the catchment monitored by that sensor, applying the catchment rule that catchments are represented as `envthes:30212` instances monitored by sensors with matching IDs. The catchment’s geometry is then used, along with the geometry of other catchments, to compute which catchments share a boundary. The temporal “1999” part requires selecting the observation from that year via `sosa:resultTime`, but the schema’s exact year-filter step is implicit in the observation chain.

